      'Turn-flow example: 1. Tableau Building: Build down in alternating colors (e.g., a Black 10 on a Red Jack).\n2. Group Moves: Any face-up card, along with all cards sitting on top of it, can be moved as a unit. The cards above the base card do NOT need to be in any specific order.\n3. Foundations: Build up in suit (A-2-3...K). Once a card is on a foundation, it usually cannot be moved back to the tableau.',
